Give each iOS touch a fresh TouchId for its lifetime, not its UITouch's address.

What: gpui_ios built a touch's `TouchId` from its `UITouch` pointer. UIKit reuses a finished touch's object, so a
later touch (the second tap of a double tap, say) came with the id of an earlier one, and GPUI could not tell them
apart (the Linux trace harness's `recorded_touches_keep_their_identity` check found it in the committed iOS traces).
`events.rs` gets `TouchIds`: the live touches by `UITouch` address; a began touch takes the next `TouchId` (from 0,
wrapping) and gives it up when it ends or is cancelled; a move or end of an address with no live touch is dropped;
a begin of an address still live cancels that stale touch, then starts its own (the rule of 0021, 0022 and 0025).
`IosWindowState` holds one; `handle_touch` sends what it returns. `touch_id` goes. Table test `touch_ids`.

Ported from flutter/flutter engine/src/flutter/lib/ui/window/pointer_data_packet_converter.cc
(`UpdatePointerIdentifier`: each down takes `++pointer_`, kept until the device's up or cancel erases its state)
and engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Source/FlutterViewController.mm (`dispatchTouches:`,
`pointer_data.device = reinterpret_cast<int64_t>(touch)`) @ 3.50.1 (ae9b586f34a8443573f82ef57c3bf914a908cbf7).
Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors. BSD-3-Clause, see third_party/flutter/LICENSE. Flutter keys a touch by its
`UITouch` pointer only while it is down and numbers pointers per down; this does the same. Left out: the rest of
the converter (synthesized add, hover and remove events; GPUI has no pointer add or remove).

Why: `TouchId` must name one touch: GPUI's recognizers, pinch arena and hit-tested touch targets all key on it.
The touch handling is private to gpui_ios, so neither a Parallax crate nor an extension trait can change it. cfg:
the crate's own (iOS).

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

